7-97704c572fae\n---\n\nDeterministic 3-stage audiobook pipeline for the LONGVIEW book output. Lives at\n`%APPDATA%/space-agent/benny-home/benny/workspaces/longview/audiobook/` (not a git repo).\n\n- `01_prepare.py` — reads `../data_out/opus/sections/p{P}c{C}s{S}.md` (72 sections, 14 chapters, 4 parts), emits `build/chapters/chNN.txt` (audiobook-clean: strips `#`/TOC and all citation forms — `(sid: hex)` ×70 is the dominant one, plus `(concept:/doc:)`, `[longview_card_xxxx]` square-bracket refs, bare `foo_bar.md` tokens → de-underscored, inline code, `$LaTeX$`; announces each Part/Chapter by voice) + `build/manifest.json` (fixed order = numeric sort of filenames).\n- `02_run_kokoro.py` — the ACTIVE driver. Calls `POST /generate` (profile_id + text, 50k cap, chunks internally) on the running backend, polls `/generate/{id}/status` (SSE `data:` lines, not plain JSON!), downloads `GET /audio/{id}` → `build/audio/chNN.wav`. Idempotent/resumable by wav presence. `02_synthesize.py` is the older MCP-path tracker (`--status/--plan/--json`), kept for reference.\n- `03_stitch.py` — stdlib `wave` concat in manifest order + inter-chapter silence gap (default 1200ms) → `build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.wav` + `build/chapters.cue.txt`. No ffmpeg. Enforces uniform wav format. Smoke-tested OK.\n\n**Voicebox is NOT the installed GUI app** — it's a SOURCE REPO at `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\voicebox` (Tauri + FastAPI, bun, `justfile`). Gemini/Antigravity ran it via `just dev`. To drive it you only need the BACKEND: `cd voicebox && backend/venv/Scripts/python -m uvicorn backend.main:app --port 17493` (venv already set up). FastAPI on `127.0.0.1:17493`; MCP mounted at `/mcp` (FastMCP Streamable-HTTP, tools `voicebox.speak/transcribe/list_profiles/list_captures`). Live DB = repo's `data/voicebox.db`. MCP registered in Claude user config (`claude mcp add --scope user --transport http voicebox http://127.0.0.1:17493/mcp`, ✓Connected) → available NEXT session, not the one that adds it.\n\nEngines & speed (this machine is **CPU-only, no GPU**): cloned `Test` voice needs `qwen` 1.7B ≈ **10× real-time → ~47h for the whole book (impractical)**. Chose **Kokoro** instead (engine `kokoro`, 82M, warm RTF ≈ **0.35× → whole book ~85 min**); created preset profile **`Narrator-Kokoro`** (voice `bm_george`, British male) via `POST /profiles {voice_type:preset,preset_engine:kokoro,preset_voice_id:bm_george}`. Trade-off: preset voice, not the clone. **Lemonade engine (`lemonade`, Kokoro-ONNX via :13305) is BROKEN** — returns ~0.3s stub audio, don't use. ~220k chars ≈ 286 min audio out. `/speak` caps text at 10k (too small for chapters); use `/generate` (50k). MP3/M4B optional post-step needs ffmpeg (not installed).\n\nPart of [[project_longview_session_synthesis]]. Status 2026-07-03: backend running, ch01 done, ch02-14 generating in background (~85 min), then `03_stitch.py`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":4,"newStart":18,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," Engines & speed (this machine is **CPU-only, no GPU**): cloned `Test` voice needs `qwen` 1.7B ≈ **10× real-time → ~47h for the whole book (impractical)**. Chose **Kokoro** instead (engine `kokoro`, 82M, warm RTF ≈ **0.35× → whole book ~85 min**); created preset profile **`Narrator-Kokoro`** (voice `bm_george`, British male) via `POST /profiles {voice_type:preset,preset_engine:kokoro,preset_voice_id:bm_george}`. Trade-off: preset voice, not the clone. **Lemonade engine (`lemonade`, Kokoro-ONNX via :13305) is BROKEN** — returns ~0.3s stub audio, don't use. ~220k chars ≈ 286 min audio out. `/speak` caps text at 10k (too small for chapters); use `/generate` (50k). MP3/M4B optional post-step needs ffmpeg (not installed)."," ","-Part of [[project_longview_session_synthesis]]. Status 2026-07-03: backend running, ch01 done, ch02-14 generating in background (~85 min), then `03_stitch.py`.","+**Shipped in prime-silo v1.11.0** (2026-07-03): workflow committed to `prime-silo/scripts/longview/audiobook/` (01_prepare/02_